 ## Overview
-This method determines the number of cells in each dimension of a uniform or two-level spatial acceleration grid based on the scene's bounding box volume and the number of geometric primitives (triangles or particles) [S1][S3, unofficial]. It solves the problem of selecting a grid resolution that balances memory usage against traversal efficiency by ensuring the cell count scales with the scene complexity [S1]. It is distinguished from [Voxel Grid Resolution Calculation](13832-voxel-grid-resolution-calculation.md) by its explicit use of a user-defined scaling factor $\lambda$ to decouple the resolution from a fixed target voxel count, allowing for dynamic adjustment based on primitive density [S1][S3, unofficial].
