 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** $O(1)$ for the resolution calculation itself. The subsequent grid construction (inserting primitives) is $O(N)$ where $N$ is the number of primitives, assuming constant-time bounding box checks [S1].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(N_x \cdot N_y \cdot N_z)$ for the grid storage. The resolution formula ensures this scales linearly with $N$ (since $N_x \propto N^{1/3}$, volume $\propto N$) [S1].
