 ## Background
-The heuristic was introduced by Cleary et al. [CWVB83] and has been widely adopted in ray tracing literature, including by Wald et al. [WIK∗ 06] [S2, unofficial]. It is based on the principle that uniform grids perform best when cell dimensions are roughly equal to the average primitive size, scaled by a factor that accounts for overlap and traversal overhead [S1].
